   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to the qualifications for holding the office of assistant district attorney in the county of Sullivan",
    "basePrintNo": "S4153",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4153-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4153\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to the\nqualifications for holding the office of assistant district attorney\nin the county of Sullivan\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThe bill authorizes Assistant District Attorneys employed by Sullivan\nCounty (other than the First Assistant District Attorney or Chief\nAssistant District Attorney) to reside within Sullivan County or an\nadjoining county within the State of New York.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nCurrent law requires assistant district attorneys employed by Sullivan\nCounty to reside within Sullivan County.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amends section 3 of the Public Officers Law to add a new\nsubdivision 66 which authorizes Assistant District Attorneys employed\nby Sullivan County (other than the First Assistant District Attorney\nor Chief Assistant District Attorney) to reside within Sullivan County\nor an adjoining county within the State of New York.\n\nSection 2: Effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis legislation was introduced at the request of the Sullivan County\nDistrict Attorney in order to increase the ability of Sullivan County\nto find and employ qualified Assistant District Attorneys. Currently\nthe following counties are allowed to employ Assistant District\nAttorneys who reside outside of the county: Essex; Fulton; Montgomery;\nPutnam; Schuyler; Wyoming; and Yates.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
